From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: app-usage: Do not collect usage with remember-app-usage off

update_enable_monitoring() says that with monitoring disabled the shell
reports usage from saved data but collects none. It only cleared the
watched app, though: the focus-app handler stays connected, so the next
focus change watched the new app again and counted its focused time,
and saved it. A person who turned off "App Usage" in Settings still had
it recorded.

Return early from the handler while monitoring is off. It must be on
before the handler runs when it is turned on, for the same reason.

--- a/src/shell-app-usage.c
+++ b/src/shell-app-usage.c
@@ -219,6 +219,9 @@
                       GParamSpec         *spec,
                       ShellAppUsage      *self)
 {
+  if (!self->enable_monitoring)
+    return;
+
   if (self->watched_app != NULL)
     increment_usage_for_app (self, self->watched_app);
 
@@ -734,6 +737,7 @@
   /* Be sure not to start the timers if they were already set */
   if (enable && !self->enable_monitoring)
     {
+      self->enable_monitoring = TRUE;
       on_focus_app_changed (shell_window_tracker_get_default (), NULL, self);
     }
   /* ...and don't try to stop them if they were not running */
